1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:05,090
Diya's homework: for two x squared
minus seven x plus three equals zero,

2
00:00:05,090 --> 00:00:08,017
find the sum and the product of the roots.

3
00:00:08,417 --> 00:00:09,724
She solved it fully.

4
00:00:09,724 --> 00:00:11,759
The roots are three and one half.

5
00:00:11,759 --> 00:00:13,294
Sum, three and a half.

6
00:00:13,294 --> 00:00:14,917
Product, one and a half.

7
00:00:15,367 --> 00:00:19,871
Aarav read the same two answers straight
off the equation, in two seconds.

8
00:00:20,221 --> 00:00:22,534
Seven over two, and three over two.

9
00:00:22,534 --> 00:00:24,664
How did he do it without solving?

10
00:00:25,164 --> 00:00:28,777
The sum and the product are
hiding inside a, b and c.

11
00:00:28,777 --> 00:00:31,992
Today: relationships between
roots and coefficients.

12
00:00:32,642 --> 00:00:33,711
First, names.

13
00:00:33,711 --> 00:00:36,173
We call the two roots alpha and beta.

14
00:00:36,523 --> 00:00:41,602
They are the two answers of a x squared
plus b x plus c equals zero, real

15
00:00:41,602 --> 00:00:43,067
or a complex pair.

16
00:00:43,467 --> 00:00:48,408
From the quadratic formula, alpha
is minus b plus root D, over two a.

17
00:00:48,808 --> 00:00:52,021
And beta is minus b
minus root D, over two a.

18
00:00:52,021 --> 00:00:54,752
Same parts, opposite sign in the middle.

19
00:00:55,402 --> 00:00:59,071
Now watch a sum stay still
while everything else moves.

20
00:00:59,071 --> 00:01:03,229
y equals x squared minus four
x plus c, with c counting up.

21
00:01:03,629 --> 00:01:07,802
The two roots slide towards each
other, but their midpoint never moves.

22
00:01:07,802 --> 00:01:09,337
It stays pinned at two.

23
00:01:09,737 --> 00:01:12,076
So their sum stays four the whole time.

24
00:01:12,076 --> 00:01:13,376
Look at the readout.

25
00:01:13,776 --> 00:01:15,472
Their product does change.

26
00:01:15,472 --> 00:01:16,695
It is exactly c.

27
00:01:16,695 --> 00:01:21,103
At c equals three, the roots are one
and three, and one times three is

28
00:01:21,103 --> 00:01:22,003
three.

29
00:01:22,081 --> 00:01:24,568
Past four, the roots become complex.

30
00:01:24,568 --> 00:01:27,928
The sum is still four: the
imaginary parts cancel.

31
00:01:28,328 --> 00:01:30,349
And the product is still c.

32
00:01:30,349 --> 00:01:35,566
At c equals five, two plus i, times
two minus i, is four minus i squared,

33
00:01:35,566 --> 00:01:36,731
which is five.

34
00:01:37,381 --> 00:01:38,281
Quick one.

35
00:01:38,245 --> 00:01:43,044
In x squared minus four x plus c,
what is the sum of the roots when c is

36
00:01:43,044 --> 00:01:44,008
one hundred?

37
00:01:44,008 --> 00:01:45,230
Pause and think.

38
00:01:48,430 --> 00:01:49,339
Still four!

39
00:01:49,339 --> 00:01:51,789
c only moves the curve up and down.

40
00:01:51,789 --> 00:01:55,148
The midpoint stays at two,
so the sum stays four.

41
00:01:55,798 --> 00:01:58,325
Now let us prove it for every quadratic.

42
00:01:58,725 --> 00:01:59,625
Step one.

43
00:01:59,539 --> 00:02:00,920
Add the two roots.

44
00:02:00,920 --> 00:02:04,497
The root D parts have opposite
signs, so they cancel.

45
00:02:05,247 --> 00:02:06,147
Step two.

46
00:02:06,125 --> 00:02:10,955
What is left is minus two b over
two a, which is minus b over a.

47
00:02:11,705 --> 00:02:12,685
Step three.

48
00:02:12,685 --> 00:02:14,155
Multiply the roots.

49
00:02:14,155 --> 00:02:19,152
A plus times a minus gives a difference
of squares: b squared minus D.

50
00:02:19,902 --> 00:02:20,802
Step four.

51
00:02:20,769 --> 00:02:21,953
Put D back in.

52
00:02:21,953 --> 00:02:25,766
b squared minus b squared
plus four a c leaves four a c.

53
00:02:25,766 --> 00:02:28,543
Over four a squared, that is c over a.

54
00:02:29,293 --> 00:02:32,218
So the sum of the roots is minus b over a.

55
00:02:32,218 --> 00:02:34,782
The product of the roots is c over a.

56
00:02:35,432 --> 00:02:39,025
These two numbers also tell
you the signs of the roots.

57
00:02:39,025 --> 00:02:40,085
Side by side.

58
00:02:40,485 --> 00:02:42,849
x squared minus five x plus six.

59
00:02:42,849 --> 00:02:45,683
Product six is positive, so same signs.

60
00:02:45,683 --> 00:02:48,516
Sum five is positive, so both positive.

61
00:02:48,516 --> 00:02:50,286
They are two and three.

62
00:02:50,686 --> 00:02:52,758
x squared plus x minus six.

63
00:02:52,758 --> 00:02:56,224
Product minus six is
negative, so opposite signs.

64
00:02:56,224 --> 00:02:58,400
They are two and minus three.

65
00:02:59,000 --> 00:02:59,903
Your turn.

66
00:02:59,903 --> 00:03:02,362
x squared minus three x minus ten.

67
00:03:02,362 --> 00:03:04,333
Can both roots be positive?

68
00:03:04,333 --> 00:03:05,660
Pause and decide.

69
00:03:08,860 --> 00:03:09,760
No!

70
00:03:09,333 --> 00:03:12,014
The product, minus ten, is negative.

71
00:03:12,014 --> 00:03:14,757
So one root is positive, one negative.

72
00:03:14,757 --> 00:03:16,821
They are five and minus two.

73
00:03:17,471 --> 00:03:18,586
Remember this.

74
00:03:18,586 --> 00:03:21,504
The sum of the roots is minus b over a.

75
00:03:21,504 --> 00:03:23,390
The product is c over a.

76
00:03:24,090 --> 00:03:25,826
Now, one worked example.

77
00:03:26,176 --> 00:03:30,607
Alpha and beta are the roots of x
squared minus five x plus three.

78
00:03:30,607 --> 00:03:33,091
Find alpha squared plus beta squared.

79
00:03:33,591 --> 00:03:34,521
Step one.

80
00:03:34,521 --> 00:03:38,378
Alpha plus beta is minus
of minus five, over one.

81
00:03:38,378 --> 00:03:39,603
That is five.

82
00:03:40,353 --> 00:03:41,273
Step two.

83
00:03:41,273 --> 00:03:43,586
Alpha beta is three over one.

84
00:03:43,586 --> 00:03:44,855
That is three.

85
00:03:45,605 --> 00:03:46,590
Step three.

86
00:03:46,590 --> 00:03:51,549
Alpha plus beta, squared, is alpha
squared plus two alpha beta plus beta

87
00:03:51,549 --> 00:03:52,449
squared.

88
00:03:52,310 --> 00:03:57,055
So alpha squared plus beta squared
is the sum squared, minus two alpha

89
00:03:57,055 --> 00:03:57,955
beta.

90
00:03:58,404 --> 00:03:59,304
Step four.

91
00:03:59,263 --> 00:04:02,560
That is twenty five minus
six, which is nineteen.

92
00:04:03,310 --> 00:04:06,303
Nineteen, without ever
finding alpha or beta.

93
00:04:06,953 --> 00:04:08,418
Now, the exam trap.

94
00:04:08,768 --> 00:04:12,117
Take two x squared minus
seven x plus three again.

95
00:04:12,117 --> 00:04:16,916
Many students write the sum as b over
a, which is minus seven over two.

96
00:04:17,316 --> 00:04:20,537
But the sum is minus b over
a: plus seven over two.

97
00:04:20,537 --> 00:04:24,301
Check with the roots: three plus
one half is three and a half.

98
00:04:24,951 --> 00:04:26,417
Where is this asked?

99
00:04:26,417 --> 00:04:30,863
In JEE Main, on expressions like
alpha squared plus beta squared, built

100
00:04:30,863 --> 00:04:34,561
from the sum and product, as
in June twenty twenty two.

101
00:04:34,561 --> 00:04:39,292
You met this in Class ten, but it is
not in the current Class eleven NCERT

102
00:04:39,292 --> 00:04:40,192
text.

103
00:04:40,443 --> 00:04:41,670
Exam level now.

104
00:04:41,670 --> 00:04:44,884
Alpha and beta are the
roots of this equation.

105
00:04:44,884 --> 00:04:48,785
Find one over alpha squared,
plus one over beta squared.

106
00:04:48,785 --> 00:04:50,064
Pause and solve.

107
00:04:55,464 --> 00:04:56,793
The answer is C.

108
00:04:56,793 --> 00:04:57,844
Eight thirds.

109
00:04:58,344 --> 00:05:01,805
Alpha plus beta is six
over two, which is three.

110
00:05:01,805 --> 00:05:03,933
Alpha beta is three over two.

111
00:05:04,433 --> 00:05:08,836
Alpha squared plus beta squared is
three squared, minus two times three

112
00:05:08,836 --> 00:05:09,736
halves.

113
00:05:09,493 --> 00:05:11,744
Nine minus three, which is six.

114
00:05:12,244 --> 00:05:16,742
Over a common denominator, that is
alpha squared plus beta squared, over

115
00:05:16,742 --> 00:05:18,248
alpha beta, squared.

116
00:05:18,248 --> 00:05:21,329
Six over nine quarters,
which is eight thirds.

117
00:05:21,929 --> 00:05:23,388
Here is your recap.

118
00:05:23,388 --> 00:05:24,888
Screenshot this card.

119
00:05:28,088 --> 00:05:30,925
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

120
00:05:31,325 --> 00:05:32,225
One.

121
00:05:31,844 --> 00:05:36,492
Find the sum and the product of the
roots of three x squared plus six x

122
00:05:36,492 --> 00:05:37,430
minus nine.

123
00:05:38,330 --> 00:05:39,230
Two.

124
00:05:38,872 --> 00:05:43,302
Why do the imaginary parts cancel
when you add a conjugate pair?

125
00:05:44,202 --> 00:05:45,102
Three.

126
00:05:44,862 --> 00:05:50,018
If alpha and beta are the roots of x
squared minus seven x plus ten, find

127
00:05:50,018 --> 00:05:52,346
alpha squared plus beta squared.

128
00:05:53,446 --> 00:05:55,433
Next time: we run it backwards.

129
00:05:55,433 --> 00:05:58,326
Give any two roots, and
we build their equation.
